.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt OECTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oectl
.Nd inspect and administer a native OpenEIGRP daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Cm show
.Ar view
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Cm clear events
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Cm version
.Nm
.Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a noninteractive client for
.Xr openeigrpd 8 .
It sends versioned, bounded requests to the local Unix management socket.
It never reads private EIGRP topology objects or the Linux kernel route
table directly.
Most commands report the daemon's current operational state;
.Cm clear events
is the only supported mutating command.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm show capabilities
Report portable release and available protocol capabilities.
.It Cm show protocols
List configured EIGRP instances and runtime status.
.It Cm show neighbors
Report neighbor state, hold time, queues, retransmissions and uptime.
.It Cm show interfaces
Report interface EIGRP settings and operational counters.
.It Cm show topology
Report DUAL prefix and path state.
.It Cm show routes
Report successors and feasible paths from the portable topology view.
This is
.Em not
a dump of the Linux kernel RIB.
.It Cm show statistics
Report portable traffic counters.
.Cm show traffic
is an alias.
.It Cm show events
Report event-log summary and entries.
.It Cm show diagnostics
Report feature capabilities, debug state and timer records.
.It Cm show tech-support
Collect the same client, host, and portable version sections as
.Cm show version ,
followed by the protocol list and available scoped read-only views.
.Cm tech-support
is an alias.
The unscoped form includes running default-VRF instances.
.It Cm clear events
Clear the event log for one running instance.
Requires root or the daemon startup UID.
.It Cm version
Show local integration release, OS, distribution, kernel, architecture
and IPC protocol version without connecting to a daemon.
.It Cm show version
Show client and host versions and an aligned portable component inventory.
Component status is read from the daemon, not inferred from the client binary.
The local
.Cm version
command does not require a running daemon.
.It Cm help
Print command usage.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s Ar path , Fl -socket Ar path
Unix management socket; default
.Pa /run/openeigrpd/control.sock .
.It Fl a Ar asn , Fl -asn Ar asn
EIGRP autonomous system number from 1 to 65535.
.It Fl 4
Select IPv4.
.It Fl 6
Select IPv6.
.It Fl -afi Ar 4|6
Select IPv4 or IPv6 using an explicit family number.
.It Fl -vrf-id Ar number
Numeric runtime VRF ID; default 0.
A nondefault VRF requires explicit ASN and AFI as well.
.It Fl -json
Output newline-delimited JSON records; this is not a single JSON array.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage.
.It Fl -version
Print local version information and exit.
.El
.Sh INSTANCE SELECTION
A scoped command can omit ASN and AFI only when there is exactly one
running default-VRF address-family instance to select.
Otherwise use
.Fl -asn
and
.Fl -afi
or
.Fl 4
or
.Fl 6 .
The protocol list exposes VRF names, not the numeric IDs needed to select
nondefault VRFs; supply
.Fl -asn ,
.Fl -afi
and
.Fl -vrf-id
together for these instances.
The current native configuration only accepts the default VRF.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Query an IPv4 AS and obtain machine-readable routes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oectl show neighbors --asn 4453 --afi 4
oectl show routes --asn 4453 --afi 4 --json
.Ed
.Pp
Query an IPv6 AS and collect diagnostics:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oectl show interfaces --asn 6473 --afi 6
oectl show diagnostics --asn 6473 --afi 6
oectl show tech-support
.Ed
.Pp
Clear only the selected instance's event history:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo oectl clear events --asn 4453 --afi 4
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT
Human-readable mode formats the daemon state into headings and view-specific
fields; JSON mode passes newline-delimited JSON records for consumers that
process one record at a time.
Tech-support JSON also includes local integration and scope records.
The daemon returns no stable cross-page snapshot; routing changes may alter
subsequent pages.
.Sh SECURITY
The control socket is normally mode 0660, with read-only access via the
.Sy openeigrpctl
group.
The daemon checks peer credentials and permits
.Cm clear events
only to root or its startup UID, regardless of socket group membership.
No interactive configuration, reload, neighbor reset or topology clearing
operation is exposed.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
IPC version 1 pages contain at most 32 records and 16 KiB; page offsets
are bounded at 8192.
A large topology may therefore produce a pagination error instead of a
complete output.
Nondefault VRF numeric IDs cannot be discovered from the protocol list.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Daemon, socket, authorization, instance selection, or protocol failure.
.It 2
Invalid command line or unsupported command.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openeigrpd 8 ,
.Xr openeigrpd.conf 5
